{
	"name": "Maintain the Shopware Novastrix Lexikon from Google Sheets",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Maintain the Shopware Novastrix Lexikon from Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\nEditors keep the shop glossary in Google Sheets. The workflow reads every row, creates missing Lexikon categories and creates or updates each entry by its term, so running it again updates the entries instead of duplicating them. Synonyms are linked in the storefront like the term itself. Invalid rows and Shopware errors, for example a term that exists twice, are written back to the sheet.\n\n### Setup\n1. Self-hosted n8n only for now: install the community node **n8n-nodes-novastrix-shopware** (tested with 0.2.0, n8n 2.48 and 3.x, Shopware 6.7) via **Settings > Community nodes**. [Installation guide](https://github.com/Breadchicken/n8n-nodes-novastrix-shopware#installation)\n2. In Shopware, create an integration under **Settings > System > Integrations** (access to the Lexikon plugin and read access to sales channels and languages) and add its access key ID and secret as a **Shopware Admin API** credential.\n3. Install the [Novastrix Lexikon](https://novastrix.com/shopware) plugin in Shopware.\n4. Connect a **Google Sheets** credential.\n5. Create a sheet with the columns `term`, `short_definition`, `description` (HTML allowed), `synonyms` (comma-separated), `category`, `status` and `message`.\n6. In **Configuration**, set the sheet URL and tab name. Optionally limit the entries to one sales channel and set the language, for example `de-DE`. Run the workflow and check the glossary in the storefront.\n\n### Customization\nReplace the manual trigger with a schedule, or add related entries and a cover image in **Create or Update Entry**.\n",
				"height": 760,
				"width": 560
			},
